So `MqttClient_Connect` calls `MqttClient_WaitType(client, &mc_connect->ack, MQTT_PACKET_TYPE_CONNECT_ACK, 0, ...)`. The `mc_connect->ack` is a `MqttConnectAck` struct. In the fuzzer, `connect` is allocated with `new MqttConnect` and then `memset(connect, 0, sizeof(*connect))`. So `connect->ack` is zeroed.

But wait - `MqttClient_WaitType` calls `MqttClient_PacketReset(packet_type, &client->msg)` which zeroes `client->msg`. But `mc_connect->ack` is a different object. Let me re-read `MqttClient_WaitType`:

In `MqttClient_WaitType`:
```c
case MQTT_MSG_BEGIN:
{
    ...
    if ((rc = MqttReadStart(client, mms_stat)) != 0) {
        return rc;
    }
    mms_stat->read = MQTT_MSG_WAIT;
}
FALL_THROUGH;

case MQTT_MSG_WAIT:
case MQTT_MSG_HEADER:
{
    /* Wait for packet */
    rc = MqttPacket_Read(client, client->rx_buf, client->rx_buf_len, timeout_ms);
    ...
    /* Decode Packet - get type, qos and id */
    rc = MqttClient_DecodePacket(client, client->rx_buf,
        client->packet.buf_len, NULL, &packet_type, &packet_qos,
        &packet_id, 1);
    ...
    MqttClient_PacketReset(packet_type, &client->msg);
    ...
    mms_stat->read = MQTT_MSG_PAYLOAD;
}
FALL_THROUGH;

case MQTT_MSG_PAYLOAD:
case MQTT_MSG_PAYLOAD2:
{
    ...
    if ((wait_type == MQTT_PACKET_TYPE_ANY ||
         wait_type == packet_type || ...) &&
        (wait_packet_id == 0 || wait_packet_id == packet_id))
    {
        use_packet_obj = packet_obj;  // This is &mc_connect->ack
        ...
    }
    ...
    rc = MqttClient_HandlePacket(client, use_packet_type, use_packet_obj, &resp, timeout_ms);
    ...
}
```

So `use_packet_obj = packet_obj = &mc_connect->ack`. This is NOT `client->msg`. `MqttClient_PacketReset` zeroes `client->msg`, not `mc_connect->ack`.

But `mc_connect->ack` was zeroed when `connect` was memset. So `props` should be NULL.

Hmm, but what about subsequent calls? After the first `MqttClient_Connect`, the `connect->ack.props` might be set to a valid prop list. Then if `MqttClient_Connect` is called again (which it isn't in the fuzzer), it would have stale props.

